aintenance and overhaul, freight and crane charges, parts sales, and other ancillary time and material-based offerings. The company was formerly known as Frontier TopCo, Inc. Kodiak Gas Services, Inc. was founded in 2010 and is headquartered in The Woodlands, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Robert M. McKee | CEO, President & Director | Age 47 | Compensation: $2.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $1.0M ranks in the below the sector median among Energy peers, with revenue growing 24%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $219K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $19K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["Kodiak Gas Services, Inc. is a mid-cap energy business with a $4.0B market cap on $1.3B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +24% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 5% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 37%.","The business throws off $284M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 22 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 7.45\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 4.1\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 2.0\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 6.6% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 2.4\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.3) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio of 113% leaves essentially no coverage if earnings wobble","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins softening -1.4pp YoY \u2014 early warning on the moat","sev":"amber","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Carries a 34% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.3396212402525065},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 8.2% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (71% sell ratio) over the past year","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.286},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 59/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; durably derated by the market \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Energy tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Geopolitical supply shocks \u2014 wars, sanctions, and OPEC decisions create volatility that no hedging programme can fully neutralise.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 10% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Growing faster than most Energy peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Energy sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 8% over 3 months"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Kodiak Gas Services, Inc. $KGS Stock Purchased by Public Sector Pension Investment Board","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"http